// A SAPIC-generated restriction that FAILS the `Formula terms` check.
//
// HS runs its wellformedness pass over the TRANSLATED theory
// (`TheoryLoader.checkTranslatedTheory`), so the `annFormulas` of
// `formulaReports` walk the `Restr_*` restrictions the `let … else` lowering
// mints, not only the restrictions the source declares.
//
// What those restrictions carry is decided by HS `rewrite`
// (Theory.Model.Restriction), which abstracts every subterm holding a free
// variable into a fresh `x` and leaves the rest verbatim:
//
//   - `<<'a'^'b', 'b'>, 'c'>` is ground, so it stays inside the restriction
//     FORMULA, and its reducible `exp` is what `checkTerms` reports;
//   - `<k, 'e'>` holds the bound-in `k`, so its restriction quantifies `x`
//     instead and is generated WITHOUT being reported — the check has to pick
//     the offender out of two candidates.
//
// Compared slices: the wf report block AND the `theory … end` echo (see
// check.sh), the latter for both generated restrictions and the
// `// safety formula` line each of them carries.

theory SapicFormulaTerms
begin

builtins: diffie-hellman

process:
  in(k);
  let <<p, q>, r> = <<'a'^'b','b'>,'c'> in
    out(<p,q,r>)
  else
    ( let <s, t> = <k, 'e'> in
        out(<s,t>)
      else
        out('no')
    )

end
